BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Entrepreneurship Mentorship Makes a Difference for All
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T200000
UID:6aaad6a2ab7a8e0037c241ef@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of Fort York Library's\nEntrepreneur in R
 esidence\n(EIR) service\nWhether you are starting a business or in job sea
 rch\, mentorship is important for newcomers in Canada. Entrepreneur in Res
 idence (Newcomer Focus)\, Jean Chow\, shares how a good mentor can bridge
  gaps and explain expectations\, real and/or perceived\, and can help newc
 omers build vital professional networks\, learn and build workplace cultur
 e\, and gain confidence.\nIn this session:\nThe Art of Mentorship – what
  is mentorship?\nDiscover mentorship programs in the GTA for entrepreneurs
 .\nStrategies on finding a great mentor/mentee.\nCome early to network fro
 m 6-6:30pm!\nTo apply for one-on-one consultations with our resident entre
 preneur\, Jean\, please fill out the in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/eir
 \n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form
  is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act
 \, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used f
 or event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abo
 ut how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline 
