BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Python Essentials 1 and 2 Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T153000
UID:6a7cd1d22dac6e00371ea5d1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn Python and build your programming skills in a supportive
  group. This learning circle will meet on Tuesday afternoons from Septemb
 er 22 to December 8\, 2-3:30pm. Learning circles are study groups guided b
 y staff for people who want to take a free online course together in a wel
 coming space. Learners meet weekly and work together through the course ma
 terials. Participants are expected to commit to the duration of the course
  and attend all learning circle sessions.\nLearners who successfully compl
 ete both courses will earn a digital badge and certificate of completion.\
 nPython Essentials 1\nis the first in a 2-course series that teaches compu
 ter programming skills including how to design\, develop\, and improve com
 puter programs using the Python programming language. The course covers es
 sential programming topics such as data types\, variables\, control flow\,
  functions\, and exceptions.\nPython Essentials 2\nis the second in a 2-co
 urse series that will prepare you for the PCAP – Certified Associate in 
 Python Programming certification exam at Pearson VUE. This intermediate-le
 vel course covers advanced aspects of Python programming\, including modul
 es\, packages\, exceptions\, file processing and object-oriented programmi
 ng (OOP).\nFor more information about the Python learning circle\, please 
 contact\nnetworkingacademy@tpl.ca\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe per
 sonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library 
 under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The i
 nformation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery
  and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information 
 can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:York Woods
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7cd1d22dac6e00371ea5d1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
